problem:
`push_base_lines` copies base's last line as it is, even when it has no final newline, and settled disk lines follow it, so two lines join. Example: base `{
  "a": 1
}` (no EOF newline), ours/theirs adding `"x"`/`"y"` before a shared `}
` (git leaves `}` settled after the block). The middle comes out as `…  "a": 1
}}
`, `line_count` says one line more than the text has, every later middle range is off by one, and applying ours over middle {2,2} drops the closing `}`.
